{
  "$comment": [
    "TASK-1050 W1 — the run-protocol v2 additions for guardrail (README §9.7.3, §9.8.1), an OVERLAY on",
    "tests/contracts/run-protocol.fixture.json: a reader merges `visibility` and `nodeScope` into the base maps and",
    "appends `examples` / `invalid` to the base lists, with the same semantics (an example passes runEventProblems",
    "with its `runKind` / `plane`; an invalid entry yields a problem containing `problem`).",
    "",
    "New PUBLIC types: `guardrail.notice` (data = a GuardrailNotice v1; envelope nodeId OPTIONAL — a consultation-",
    "level notice has no node) and `run.paused` (data {reason:'guardrail_hold', noticeId, nodeId}; a run-level event,",
    "so the node rides in data). `guardrail.inbound|outbound` (admin) gain action WARN|IGNORE and checks[] (no content).",
    "`run.completed` gains guardrailNotices?: GuardrailNotice[]. GUARDRAIL_BLOCKED stays as the run error code.",
    "Notice cross-field rules: action === typeAction[type]; messageKey starts with `<type>.`; defaultMessage is EXACTLY",
    "the fixed label of messageKey (from guardrail-vocabulary.fixture.json) — never free text, so a notice can never",
    "echo PHI or the injection itself.",
    "Readers: packages/async-contract (TS, this lane), packages/agentic-sdk-v2 + packages/vox-node (W2d),",
    "apps/harness run_protocol.py (W2f), apps/admin-console shared/sandbox/api/run-protocol.ts (W3b)."
  ],
